WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.970
Man, I'm tired.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:14.910
Oh no...

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:20.380
My heart aches.

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:22.040
Excuse me.

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:27.040
Mr. Mashiko! I thought I told you to knock before coming in!

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:30.840
I did. You just didn't notice.

00:00:31.510 --> 00:00:33.050
Just what were you doing, anyway?

00:00:33.050 --> 00:00:35.120
I was reading!

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:38.010
Do you really need to hide what you were reading that badly?

00:00:38.010 --> 00:00:39.760
It's not like that!

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:42.040
Whatever.

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:46.250
Oh, that's right. The principal was looking for you.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:47.020
Okay.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.370
Mr. Mashiko?

00:00:49.370 --> 00:00:50.150
Yeah?

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.700
Don't peek!

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:54.790
You're not going to open it up, right?

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:56.030
Didn't plan on it.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:58.280
All right, I'm going now.

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:06.960
Now I'm curious.

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:13.970
April 26th

00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:16.890
One, two, three, four!

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:19.140
Two, two, three, four!

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.390
One, two, three, four!

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:23.640
Two, two, three, four!

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:25.900
One, two, three, four!

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:28.280
Two, two, three, four!

00:01:28.280 --> 00:01:30.400
One, two, three, four!

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.320
Two, two, three, four!

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:34.700
Good morning!

00:01:34.700 --> 00:01:36.280
You wanna join in, Nazuna?

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:38.280
Morning, Nazuna.

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:39.780
Good morning.

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:40.680
Good morning!

00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:41.660
Come on, join in!

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.310
Can I?

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:46.670
Of course!

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:49.420
All right, one, two, three, four!

00:01:49.420 --> 00:01:51.630
Two, two, three, four!

00:01:51.650 --> 00:01:53.670
One, two, three, four!

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.180
Two, two, three, four!

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:07.440
Good morning, class.

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:11.940
I'm in a wonderful mood today!

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:20.240
The sky is blue, the gardens are abloom with pretty flowers, and I just feel so bubbly!

00:02:20.260 --> 00:02:23.200
I want you all to feel like this too!

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:30.460
I know! For art class today, we'll go looking for spring!

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:35.000
Bring your sketchbook and a subject, and let's meet up outside!

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.220
Such a vivid imagination...

00:02:37.220 --> 00:02:38.720
Spring

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:41.970
I wonder what's up with Miss Yoshinoya.

00:02:41.970 --> 00:02:43.220
Isn't it because it's spring?

00:02:43.220 --> 00:02:48.230
I kind of remember her being like this last fall too.

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.810
Oh, that!

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:55.820
October 15th

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:55.820
"The Lofty Sky, the Shady Trees"

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.610
Art Dept.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:14.920
Good morning, class.

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:18.670
Today, I'm struck with melancholy.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:22.180
I can't calm my heart.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:27.430
Do you believe in love at first sight?

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:31.060
Or are you still too young for that?

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.060
She's starting this early?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.500
I wonder what's up with her.

00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.910
I dunno.

00:03:37.910 --> 00:03:39.570
I guess because it's fall.

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:57.050
Today, let's try to find fall!

00:03:57.050 --> 00:04:00.540
The atmosphere and lighting are different than summer.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:02.430
Try to incorporate that in your sketches.

00:04:02.430 --> 00:04:05.800
I'll be going around checking on you.

00:04:05.800 --> 00:04:07.180
Okay.

00:04:14.690 --> 00:04:17.200
She's checking her phone again?

00:04:18.890 --> 00:04:21.180
She seems worried about something.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:22.620
Yeah.

00:04:23.260 --> 00:04:24.530
I can't really tell what.

00:04:33.170 --> 00:04:35.540
Miya's sketch has a great feel to it!

00:04:35.540 --> 00:04:39.200
I'm drawn to the shadows, rather than the subject itself.

00:04:39.200 --> 00:04:41.800
I can't see that in mine.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:44.800
I wonder if it's fall enough.

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.620
The lofty sky makes it feel like fall.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.860
Thanks. I'll polish it a little more.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:53.190
Me too!

00:05:03.100 --> 00:05:08.580
The lofty sky... It feels so depressing watching them alone.

00:05:09.470 --> 00:05:11.330
Miss Yoshinoya?

00:05:11.770 --> 00:05:13.430
It's nothing!

00:05:13.430 --> 00:05:17.080
You've both done well bringing out the feel of fall.

00:05:19.320 --> 00:05:22.380
It's nice! Keep going.

00:05:23.450 --> 00:05:24.630
Tears?

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.880
Hello, Miss Yoshinoya.

00:05:37.910 --> 00:05:41.020
Oh, hello Natsume.

00:05:54.790 --> 00:05:56.820
Oh, she was doing that?

00:05:56.820 --> 00:05:59.370
Yeah, that's weird.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:01.800
I wonder what happened to her.

00:06:01.800 --> 00:06:03.800
You're also worried, Hiro?

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.050
Aren't you? How about you, Miya?

00:06:09.550 --> 00:06:14.230
Yeah, but she must have some reason.

00:06:14.230 --> 00:06:16.190
Yeah, you're right.

00:06:16.190 --> 00:06:17.600
Hold on.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:19.950
Let's review our information.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:23.660
She's worried and keeps checking her phone.

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.790
She keeps saying odd things about "the one," "sadness,"

00:06:25.790 --> 00:06:29.120
and "not being able to calm her heart."

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.200
She's emotionally unstable.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:34.950
As an author, what are your thoughts?

00:06:34.950 --> 00:06:36.710
She's in love.

00:06:37.560 --> 00:06:38.460
Love?

00:06:38.970 --> 00:06:39.960
Love!?

00:06:39.960 --> 00:06:42.250
And it's one-sided.

00:06:42.270 --> 00:06:45.710
It's probably all she can think about.

00:06:45.710 --> 00:06:46.840
No way.

00:06:46.840 --> 00:06:49.550
Hey, aren't you going to eat?

00:06:53.580 --> 00:06:56.640
You sure know everything about love, Sae.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:06:58.200
No I d—

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:02.020
I mean, anyone could think of that.

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.020
We can't be sure yet.

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:09.280
Hm, I wonder. This just started yesterday, right?

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.530
Yeah, it was sudden.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:14.910
She's in love? What do we do? What do we do?

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:18.120
I don't think you can do anything about it, Yunocchi.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.040
How should I act in class this afternoon?

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:24.920
If it's true, I wonder who it could be.

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.050
Who?

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:29.300
Well, she can't be in love with herself.

00:07:29.310 --> 00:07:31.550
She must be waiting for someone to text her.

00:07:35.170 --> 00:07:37.060
It must be a bittersweet love.

00:07:38.770 --> 00:07:41.940
Has anyone seen Miss Yoshinoya?

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.480
She was in the library earlier.

00:07:47.480 --> 00:07:49.860
I see. Thank you.

00:07:49.860 --> 00:07:53.200
If you see her again, be sure to tell me.

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:59.200
She seems to have lost her ability to be a teacher somewhere.

00:08:05.820 --> 00:08:07.090
Sob, sob.

00:08:07.620 --> 00:08:08.960
Sob, sob.

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.610
Lunch is over, Miss Yoshinoya.

00:08:16.610 --> 00:08:20.350
But I have nowhere to go!

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:24.980
You're a teacher. You can't hide in the nurse's cot.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:27.740
But I want to see how it ends!

00:08:27.740 --> 00:08:30.050
You'll get the principal angry again.

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:33.480
He's always too angry at me!

00:08:34.620 --> 00:08:40.330
Hey, Miss Kuwahara, do you believe in love at first sight?

00:08:40.350 --> 00:08:43.210
It'd be a bit inconvenient to go head-over-heels like that.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:48.750
Okay, reading time is over.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.180
I was just at the best part!

00:08:53.180 --> 00:08:55.120
Whatever, just put your phone away.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.310
If you don't hurry, you won't make it in time.

00:08:58.050 --> 00:08:59.850
But I wanna see what happens!

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:04.980
Miss Kuwahara, is love true?

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:11.110
Mr. Mashiko! How many times have I told you to knock before you come in!?

00:09:11.110 --> 00:09:12.860
This is the nurse's office.

00:09:12.860 --> 00:09:14.860
That doesn't matter!

00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:21.500
Here you go, thanks.

00:09:22.080 --> 00:09:24.510
What's up with Miss Yoshinoya?

00:09:24.510 --> 00:09:26.000
Dunno.

00:09:33.510 --> 00:09:36.890
Miss Yoshinoya seems really on edge.

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:40.140
Yeah, she rushed through the final homeroom.

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:45.810
Have your sketches from today ready to present tomorrow morning, class.

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:49.560
That's all for homeroom. Goodbye.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:52.990
I wonder what's wrong.  I'm worried.

00:09:54.190 --> 00:09:56.740
Miya, look! Isn't that Miss Yoshinoya?

00:09:57.740 --> 00:09:59.200
What's she doing?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:01.120
I hope it's nothing dangerous.

00:10:02.990 --> 00:10:04.830
I think she's looking at something.

00:10:04.830 --> 00:10:06.200
Her phone again!?

00:10:06.200 --> 00:10:07.720
What do we do, Miya!?

00:10:07.710 --> 00:10:09.330
Want to go check?

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.670
What's wrong, Yuno? Did you forget something?

00:10:14.670 --> 00:10:17.930
Hiro! Miss Yoshinoya is—

00:10:26.280 --> 00:10:28.240
Miss Yoshinoya is what?

00:10:28.240 --> 00:10:29.020
Beats me.

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:40.530
Miss Yoshinoya! Don't do anything rash!

00:10:41.120 --> 00:10:42.950
Yuno, everyone...

00:10:44.580 --> 00:10:46.830
What are you doing?

00:10:46.830 --> 00:10:48.960
We were wondering the same thing about you.

00:10:48.960 --> 00:10:50.580
You're up here with your phone.

00:10:50.580 --> 00:10:52.090
My phone?

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.330
Oh!

00:10:54.830 --> 00:10:57.090
It's <i>Love Is True.</i>

00:10:59.090 --> 00:11:01.430
<i>Love Is True?</i>

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:04.680
That popular new phone novel, right?

00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:06.580
You've heard of it, Sae?

00:11:06.580 --> 00:11:08.680
It's really interesting.

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:11.190
I can't stop wondering how it will end!

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:15.070
Sorry, I'm gonna go back to reading.

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:18.070
Take care on your way home, okay?

00:11:18.070 --> 00:11:20.570
Goodbye, Miss Yoshinoya.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:22.820
Goodbye.

00:11:27.940 --> 00:11:29.830
A phone novel, huh?

00:11:29.830 --> 00:11:32.580
I've never read one of those.

00:11:32.580 --> 00:11:37.510
Sorry. I took things totally the wrong way.

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:41.640
No, it's my fault for saying that at lunch.

00:11:41.640 --> 00:11:44.760
But I'm glad we know what it is now.

00:11:44.760 --> 00:11:47.180
I haven't read one either.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.600
It must be a lot of work having a phone.

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:53.610
I guess it is.

00:11:53.610 --> 00:11:56.480
If it's that interesting, then maybe I should read it too.

00:12:06.450 --> 00:12:09.080
There it is! <i>Love Is True.</i>

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:11.790
The lofty sky, and the shady trees...

00:12:11.790 --> 00:12:15.040
If he isn't there, it all fades to gray.

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:19.550
Strolling side by side under the trees, sitting together on a bench...

00:12:19.550 --> 00:12:23.800
I can still remember the night of my first kiss.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:27.060
Could this be true love?

00:12:27.870 --> 00:12:31.560
My heart pounding so hard I could collapse...

00:12:31.560 --> 00:12:36.230
But you embraced me gently, Nao.

00:12:39.190 --> 00:12:41.950
I don't get it.

00:12:42.470 --> 00:12:44.200
Good night.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:48.950
October 15th

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:48.950
The end

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:48.950
To be continued

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:53.960
April 26th~27th

00:12:48.970 --> 00:12:53.960
Experienced in Love

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:59.380
Yunocchi, hurry up!

00:13:00.350 --> 00:13:02.880
I'm not gonna have time to change!

00:13:05.310 --> 00:13:06.640
Okay, set!

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:08.640
All right, let's run!

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:09.560
Yeah!

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:19.340
Catch me if you can!

00:13:19.320 --> 00:13:21.110
Miya, wait!

00:13:25.920 --> 00:13:27.490
We're gonna be late!

00:13:27.490 --> 00:13:29.410
Come on, Miya...

00:13:30.660 --> 00:13:32.160
Nazuna spotted!

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:34.790
Oh, yeah, you're right.

00:13:35.230 --> 00:13:36.790
I wonder what she's doing.

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:39.750
Carrying teaching materials?

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:43.300
So, Nazuna is in charge of boxes?

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:44.930
In charge of boxes?

00:13:50.930 --> 00:13:54.640
I wonder how Nazuna's doing in her classes.

00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:58.900
You know how she's so reserved.

00:13:58.900 --> 00:14:03.500
I don't even know what kind of people are in Gen Ed.

00:14:03.500 --> 00:14:07.660
Well, it's Gen Ed, so I'm sure they're normal.

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:11.160
Normal people?

00:14:11.700 --> 00:14:12.910
Like me!

00:14:19.380 --> 00:14:23.210
Want to go to Sekaiya the day after tomorrow? I need more colors of gouache.

00:14:23.210 --> 00:14:25.350
Yeah, me too.

00:14:25.340 --> 00:14:26.220
Hey, Sae...

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:28.640
Isn't that Nazuna?

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:29.840
Nazuna?

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.310
Doesn't it seem...

00:14:35.810 --> 00:14:38.350
...a little tense between them?

00:14:39.850 --> 00:14:42.020
Hey, Sae?

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:43.110
Sae?

00:14:50.370 --> 00:14:54.450
I saw Nazuna walking with a boy earlier!

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:57.960
It looked like he was helping her carry something heavy.

00:14:59.370 --> 00:15:02.710
We saw them during recess too.

00:15:02.710 --> 00:15:03.960
The one in glasses?

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.840
No, he had a crew cut.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.130
Hm, I wonder.

00:15:09.130 --> 00:15:12.050
Maybe Nazuna's popular with the boys?

00:15:13.830 --> 00:15:15.850
Popular with the boys?

00:15:17.080 --> 00:15:20.310
That's popular? I don't get it.

00:15:20.980 --> 00:15:22.440
Sae?

00:15:27.190 --> 00:15:29.320
Why don't we go ask Norippe?

00:15:29.320 --> 00:15:31.320
Yes, let's.

00:15:38.410 --> 00:15:39.830
Popular with the boys?

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:43.080
Yeah, you might be right.

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:46.300
Our classes are on the same floor, so I see her a lot.

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:48.720
Sometimes, she's with boys.

00:15:49.300 --> 00:15:54.310
She's been watering the flower beds lately, and one time, there were three boys there.

00:15:55.260 --> 00:15:58.980
And then another time, there were four ladybugs!

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:01.060
That's not quite what we meant, but still pretty amazing.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:04.950
All right, let's go see Nazuna!

00:16:04.950 --> 00:16:06.150
See her?

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:15.580
Nazuna, you here?

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:17.020
Coming!

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.790
There's something you need to tell us.

00:16:26.040 --> 00:16:28.550
How about at least showing us?

00:16:33.550 --> 00:16:36.680
Nazuna, have you ever gotten a love letter?

00:16:37.880 --> 00:16:40.590
Um... In kindergarten.

00:16:40.590 --> 00:16:41.810
Wow, she's an early bloomer!

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:46.310
Then have you ever shared an ice cream cone with a boy?

00:16:46.310 --> 00:16:49.980
Um... That was in kindergarten too, I think.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:51.760
An early bloomer!

00:16:52.320 --> 00:16:56.450
When was the first time you ate green tea ice cream?

00:16:56.450 --> 00:16:59.910
Um... That was in first grade.

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:01.200
Definitely an early bloomer!

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:03.620
What was that last one supposed to mean?

00:17:08.890 --> 00:17:10.920
Sorry to ask you so much.

00:17:10.920 --> 00:17:13.770
We just saw you taking out the trash today

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:17.140
and thought you might be popular with the boys.

00:17:17.140 --> 00:17:18.970
Huh? No way.

00:17:19.420 --> 00:17:21.270
We saw you at recess too.

00:17:23.020 --> 00:17:27.940
Well, boys help me out from time to time, but...

00:17:27.940 --> 00:17:29.360
Wow!

00:17:30.170 --> 00:17:31.610
There's nothing to be amazed about!

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.750
I don't like it!

00:17:33.750 --> 00:17:35.240
Really?

00:17:35.240 --> 00:17:38.990
My curry is full of carrots.

00:17:39.470 --> 00:17:40.870
What is she talking about?

00:17:42.640 --> 00:17:48.250
When boys help me out, the girls they're friendly with get mad at me.

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:55.430
That happened a lot in elementary and middle school.

00:17:56.050 --> 00:18:02.100
But I'm still grateful for their help, so I don't want to turn it down.

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.350
And then they get jealous?

00:18:04.350 --> 00:18:07.230
It's not all bad, though, right?

00:18:07.810 --> 00:18:11.150
That's right, I'm sure there are good things about it.

00:18:14.780 --> 00:18:16.280
Carrot

00:18:15.160 --> 00:18:18.780
I guess I can eat my carrots.

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:21.370
Maybe she's more optimistic than we thought?

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:29.000
It's still strange. Why you, Nazuna?

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:33.510
You're not anything like what I'd imagine a popular girl to be.

00:18:33.510 --> 00:18:36.560
I'm thinking a bright, energetic personality, loads of talent,

00:18:36.560 --> 00:18:41.640
and a little ditziness, with a nice style, you know?

00:18:46.640 --> 00:18:48.030
What?

00:18:49.980 --> 00:18:52.150
That was an interesting conversation.

00:18:52.150 --> 00:18:54.300
It was pretty random.

00:19:00.230 --> 00:19:01.500
Nazuna!

00:19:01.500 --> 00:19:03.280
Are you going to sneeze? Hold it in!

00:19:09.290 --> 00:19:12.000
No wonder they can't leave her alone.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:14.770
Sorry to stay so long.

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:16.420
No problem, come again.

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:18.080
See you next week!

00:19:18.080 --> 00:19:19.300
Next week?

00:19:19.940 --> 00:19:20.930
Good night.

00:19:21.050 --> 00:19:22.390
Good night.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:23.780
Good night.

00:19:25.470 --> 00:19:27.700
Nori, do you have a minute?

00:19:29.230 --> 00:19:32.730
Are you angry about before?

00:19:32.730 --> 00:19:36.280
You know, when I said you weren't like what I imagined a popular girl to be.

00:19:40.740 --> 00:19:43.830
I see, so that's how you solve it!

00:19:43.830 --> 00:19:47.540
I thought a girl in Gen Ed would be better at studying than me.

00:19:48.000 --> 00:19:52.040
You can draw and study. You're really amazing.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:56.300
I'm not that great.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:20:01.160
Well, if there's anything I can help you with, just ask.

00:20:01.160 --> 00:20:03.220
Really? Thanks!

00:20:14.760 --> 00:20:16.360
Good morning.

00:20:16.490 --> 00:20:17.860
Good morning.

00:20:18.280 --> 00:20:18.990
Huh?

00:20:18.990 --> 00:20:22.740
Miss Yoshinoya, what did you do with your hair?

00:20:22.950 --> 00:20:26.490
Didn't you know, Miss Kuwahara?

00:20:27.070 --> 00:20:30.540
This is the hot new hairstyle!

00:20:30.950 --> 00:20:32.040
Hot?

00:20:32.040 --> 00:20:33.830
It's hot.

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.960
Where did she hear about that?

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.960
April 26th~27th

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.960
The end

00:20:36.960 --> 00:20:39.960
To be continued

00:20:40.790 --> 00:20:43.970
Yoohoo! I'm the one and only Miyakonosuke!

00:20:43.970 --> 00:20:46.220
Miya, what are you doing all of a sudden!?

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:48.610
Maybe she wants to hear a story about kabuki?

00:20:48.610 --> 00:20:52.660
"If you're far away, listen up! If you're near me, watch this!" huh?

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:56.450
You've got to say that right after you introduce yourself.

00:20:56.450 --> 00:20:58.510
But starting got me too hungry.

00:20:58.510 --> 00:21:01.610
It must be tough being you, Miyako.

00:21:01.620 --> 00:21:05.610
Next time, "May 3rd~4th: A Day in Seven Parts."

00:21:05.610 --> 00:21:09.240
We'll be waiting at Hidamari Apartments. Be sure to come see us!
